    "title": "Publix confirms new Georgetown location - NewsBreak",
    "text": "GEORGETOWN, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — Georgetown is getting a Publix. The company said it has executed a lease on a location at Elkhorn Village Center on the southwest corner of Frankfort Road and McClelland Circle. It’s going to be a 50,325-square-foot Publix Super Market and an adjacent Publix Liquors that will employ 150 people. “We are excited to continue our growth across Kentucky with a new location in Georgetown,” media relations manager Jared Glover said. “We look forward to our new customers experiencing the Publix difference soon.” As of now, there is no timeframe for an opening. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.",
